<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO appoints new Asia Pacific chief.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO appoints new Asia Pacific chief.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO NV said on Tuesday that Ton de Boer had been appointed chief executive of ABN AMRO Asia Pacific region in Singapore effective today.</p>
<p>He was previously vice-chairman of ABN AMRO North America Inc in Chicago.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO said de Boer would supervise the bank's &quot;Asia 2000&quot; strategy under which it would invest an extra $1.0 billion and double staff in the region to some 6,000 by early next century.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO is represented in 17 countries in the Asia Pacific region, where its history dates back to 1826.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
